              (ii)   after the Table and the entries  “NA-Not Applicable”, the following shall be inserted,
               namely:-
               “$For poultry meat the requirement shall be applicable for Salmonella enterica serovars
               Typhi, Typhimurium and Entritidis”;

               (iii)  after the explanatory note and the entries relating thereto “Stage where the Microbiological
               Standards shall apply”, following entry shall be inserted, namely:-

             “The Microbiological Standards in Table-5B (Food Safety Criteria) define the acceptability
                of a batch/lot and shall be met in respect of the product at the end of the manufacturing
               process and the products in the market during their shelf- life.”;

            (iv)  under the explanatory note relating to “Action in case of unsatisfactory result”, for the
                portion beginning with the words,  figures and  letters “Ensure  that  all food  safety
                 criteria”and ending with the words “the products in the market during their shelf-life’’, the
               following shall be substituted, namely:-

               ‘‘Ensure that all food safety criteria’s specified in Table-5B are complied with’’,

            (v)  under the explanatory note relating to “sampling plans and Guidelines’’, -

         (A)  in the heading “For Regulator” before the words “The final decision shall be drawn”, the
               following shall be inserted, namely:-

           “A set (n) of five samples shall be tested from three different accredited laboratories and
                the final decision shall be drawn based on three test results. There will be no provision for
                 retesting or re-sampling for microbiological testing”;

          (B) in the heading relating to ‘‘Reference Test Methods”,-

                     (i) in the entry ,after the words ‘‘shall apply’’, the following shall be inserted, namely: -

               “Test  methods  prescribed  in FSSAI Manual  of  Methods  of  Analysis  of  Foods
               (Microbiological Testing) may also be referred along with the IS/ISO methods specified
                 for Process Hygiene Criteria and Food Safety Criteria.”;

                     (ii) in the Table, against. S.No. 9, under column 2 relating to Parameter, for the entry,
               “Clostridium perfringens” the following entry shall be substituted, namely:-

                “Clostridium botulinum”.

